step 8 - HN API fallback (3 triggers) - 2026-09-24

Problem: news.ycombinator.com answers HTTP 419 "Sorry" from Cloudflare
Workers IPs (production). Empty parse would also happen if HN changes
its tr.athing / .titleline markup.

Solution: backend/src/services/HackerNewsScraper.js now keeps cheerio
HTML as primary source and falls back to the official HN API
(https://hacker-news.firebaseio.com/v0) when ANY of these triggers fires:
  1. network error (fetch rejects)
  2. non-OK HTTP status (e.g. 419)
  3. HTML parses to zero entries (markup change)

Fallback mapping: topstories.json ids -> item/<id>.json ->
  number = position in topstories, title = item.title,
  points = item.score (default 0), comments = item.descendants (default 0)
Deleted/unusable items are skipped and survivors renumbered.
Subrequests per fallback: 1 + 30 = 31 (free plan limit: 50).
Traceability: console.log "[scraper] HTML source unavailable (...); using
official HN API" and scraper.lastSource = 'html' | 'api' | null.

If BOTH sources fail -> 500 with combined message:
  "Failed to fetch Hacker News from HTML and API. HTML: ... API: ..."

Test Files  10 passed (10)
     Tests  123 passed (123)   [115 before + 8 new fallback tests]
   Duration  5.51s

Verbose highlights (tests/HackerNewsScraper.test.js - 22 passed):
  scrape > throws an error when the response is not ok                  -> lastSource null, both sources fail, combined error
  scrape > falls back to the official HN API when the HTML fetch returns 419
  scrape > falls back to the official HN API when the fetch rejects with a network error
  scrape > falls back to the official HN API when HTML parses to zero entries
  scrape > uses the HTML source without calling the API when parsing succeeds (fetcher called once)
  scrape > throws a combined error when both the HTML and API sources fail
  scrape > maps API items to number, title, points and comments with 0 defaults
  scrape > skips deleted or failing API items and renumbers the survivors
  scrape > throws when the API returns no usable items

Fallback logs captured during the run:
  [scraper] HTML source unavailable (Failed to fetch Hacker News: 419 Sorry); using official HN API
  [scraper] HTML source unavailable (fetch failed); using official HN API
  [scraper] HTML source unavailable (HTML parsed to zero entries); using official HN API
